cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "RegReady: AI-Powered Regulatory Risk & Compliance Tool for Product Teams"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Del
    family-names: Schlangen
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-5116-9564"
repository-code: "https://github.com/delschlangen/regready"
url: "https://reg-ready.vercel.app/"
abstract: >-
  RegReady turns regulatory complexity into engineering clarity, helping
  product and engineering teams ship compliant AI products without deciphering
  200-page statutes. It provides a regulatory radar for tracking new
  developments, a translator that converts legal text into engineering
  requirements, a risk scorer that evaluates AI product features against global
  regulatory frameworks (EU AI Act, NIST AI RMF, US state and federal law), and
  a SAIF mapper that maps regulatory obligations to Google's Secure AI Framework.
keywords:
  - ai-regulation
  - compliance
  - eu-ai-act
  - nist-ai-rmf
  - regtech
  - risk-assessment
  - saif
  - governance
  - responsible-ai
